+## TL;DR
+- `gitroomhq/postiz-app` is the strongest GitHub-native social scheduling choice in this niche if you want a product that actually looks like a social media manager workflow.
+- `activepieces/activepieces`, `browser-use/browser-use`, and `unclecode/crawl4ai` are the most useful automation layer for repurposing content, scraping trends, and building repeatable publishing pipelines.
+- `ollama/ollama`, `FlowiseAI/Flowise`, `danny-avila/LibreChat`, and `Mintplex-Labs/anything-llm` are the fastest way to stand up private AI copilots for caption drafts, briefs, hooks, and idea generation.
+- `Comfy-Org/ComfyUI`, `AUTOMATIC1111/stable-diffusion-webui`, `invoke-ai/InvokeAI`, and `lllyasviel/Fooocus` cover most open source image-generation needs for campaign mockups and post creatives.
+- Audio, subtitle, and talking-avatar workflows are best covered by `openai/whisper`, `coqui-ai/TTS`, `SWivid/F5-TTS`, `facefusion/facefusion`, and `OpenTalker/SadTalker`.
+
+## Why This List
+Open source matters for social teams because content operations move fast, budgets change, and compliance requirements usually arrive after tooling decisions have already been made. A strong list of the best AI tools for social media managers should therefore favor repos you can inspect, fork, self-host, automate, and connect to your own publishing stack. This list also filters out closed SaaS products and source-available projects with unclear fit when better GitHub-first alternatives exist.
+
