+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for social media managers in 2026?
+If you need the shortest answer, start with Postiz for scheduling, Activepieces for automation, Ollama plus LibreChat for drafting, ComfyUI or Fooocus for visuals, and Whisper for subtitles. Those six repos cover the most common day-to-day workflows with public GitHub URLs and self-hosting paths.
+
+### Are there any free AI social media management tools on GitHub that are not SaaS products?
+Yes. This list deliberately excludes closed SaaS products and points only to public GitHub repos. Some projects offer hosted businesses alongside the repo, but the recommendation here is always the repository itself, not the paid cloud tier.
+
+### Which GitHub repo is best for AI social media scheduling?
+`gitroomhq/postiz-app` is the closest direct match because it is explicitly built as a social media scheduling tool with AI features. General workflow tools like Activepieces and Huginn are better when you want custom automations around publishing rather than a ready-made scheduler.
+
+### What is the best open source stack for generating social media captions and post ideas?
+A practical stack is `ollama/ollama` for local model runtime, `danny-avila/LibreChat` or `janhq/jan` for a usable interface, and `Mintplex-Labs/anything-llm` when you need brand documents and campaign briefs in the loop. Add Flowise when you want reusable prompt workflows instead of ad hoc prompting.
+
+### Which open source GitHub tools help with AI image generation for social media creatives?
+For node-based control use ComfyUI. For a mature web UI use AUTOMATIC1111. For faster, easier prompting use Fooocus. For more professional iterative workflows use InvokeAI. For enhancement and cleanup, pair them with Upscayl, Real-ESRGAN, rembg, or IOPaint.
+
+### Are there open source AI tools on GitHub for subtitles, voiceovers, and talking avatars?
+Yes. Whisper handles transcription and subtitles, Coqui TTS and F5-TTS handle speech generation, and SadTalker plus FaceFusion cover avatar-style or synthetic presenter workflows. This category is improving, but it is still smaller than image-generation tooling, which is why deeper curation matters.
+
+### Why are some well-known AI repos missing from this list?
+This repo uses stricter inclusion rules than a typical awesome list. If a project lacked a clear GitHub repo fit, relied too heavily on proprietary SaaS positioning, or used licensing terms that were weaker than the rest of the field for this use case, it was left out to keep the list defensible.
